/*
  IRBlaster – ESP32 firmware for controlling air conditioners and TVs
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Hebrew web UI at http://irblaster.local (iPhone/PC) or the device IP;
    installable to the home screen (PWA)
  - Easy setup: the IR_WIFI portal connects to home WiFi and then shows the
    remote's address with a button to open it
  - AC: full control (power/mode/temp/fan/swing) via IRremoteESP8266's IRac,
    with auto-detect from the original remote, or "learned scenes" for
    unsupported units (e.g. many Israeli Electra/Tadiran = KELON168)
  - TV: built-in code sets for 20 brands (Samsung, LG, TCL, Hisense, Xiaomi,
    Sony, Philips, Toshiba, Panasonic, Sharp, ...) from Flipper-IRDB (CC0),
    auto-detect from the original remote, "test code" wizard, and a wizard that
    learns a whole remote key by key
  - "My buttons": learn any IR button and replay it
  - Quick access: one-tap import for the Android app "HTTP Shortcuts"
    (Quick Settings tile) and ready URLs for iPhone Shortcuts / Control Center
  - OTA: /update (and /u) web upload of a .bin
  - Security: per-device API key (blocks CSRF from web pages), Host-header
    check (blocks DNS rebinding), optional admin password (Basic auth) for
    firmware update / pins / WiFi reset, no firmware update from the open
    IR_WIFI network

  Project layout (open IRBlaster.ino in Arduino IDE):
    src/IRremoteESP8266/  vendored library (v2.9.0, LGPL-2.1) with only the
                          protocols we need – see tools/config_ir_lib.py
    tv_codes.h            generated by tools/gen_tv_codes.py
    web/ + web_assets.h   UI pages; after editing web/ run tools/build_web.py
  Board: "ESP32 Dev Module", partition "Default 4MB with spiffs".
  No extra libraries need to be installed.
*/

